SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] swimming — 2\,500–3\,000m total: warm-up drills\,
  one 1\,000m continuous bl
DESCRIPTION:2\,500–3\,000m total: warm-up drills\, one 1\,000m continuous
  block @ 2:30/100m\, then 4×200m @ 2:25/100m with full rest — reduce co
 ntinuous block length given low swim base\n\nReason: With only ~2km of swi
 mming logged in the past 4 weeks\, a 2\,000m continuous block 15 days befo
 re the race is a large aerobic demand on an underprepared swimmer\; halvin
 g the continuous block still builds race-specific feel without the injury 
 or fatigue cost.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-31
